### Object Interactions: Selection, Dragging, Scaling, Rotation, Skewing

Fabric’s interactive `Canvas` enables these by default. Control them per-object with flags and control visibility. See docs: Core concepts → Interactions; Configuring controls.

```ts
// Enable/disable interactions per object
rect.selectable = true; // selection
rect.evented = true; // pointer events
rect.hasControls = true; // show control handles

// Dragging
rect.lockMovementX = false;
rect.lockMovementY = false;

// Scaling and rotation
rect.lockScalingFlip = true; // prevent negative-scale flips
rect.lockRotation = false;

// Skewing (set programmatically as needed)
rect.skewX = 0;
rect.skewY = 0;

// Control handle visibility
rect.setControlsVisibility({
  mt: true, // middle top (scale Y)
  mb: true,
  ml: true, // middle left (scale X)
  mr: true,
  tl: true, // corners
  tr: true,
  bl: true,
  br: true,
  mtr: true, // rotation control
});

canvas.requestRenderAll();
```

Basic interaction events:

```ts
canvas.on("selection:created", (e) => {
  // e.selected contains selected objects
});

canvas.on("object:modified", (e) => {
  // e.target is the modified object
});

canvas.on("mouse:down", (e) => {
  // e.target if an object was clicked
});
```

